# The security audit, before the push rather than after it.
#
# It is the one gate nobody runs by hand, and it is cheap: a few seconds against the registry, over
# every lockfile in the repository. A vulnerable transitive dependency reached a published starter
# because nothing local looked, and the root's overrides do not reach a nested lockfile.
#
# Everything else worth running before a push is `pnpm run verify`, which is slower and stays a
# choice. This hook blocks only on an advisory, and `--no-verify` is there when you need it.
pnpm run audit:ci
